{"resourceIdentifier":"4667","resourceName":"TTCA ORGANIC COMPOSTING PROJECT IN ATTAPEU","description":"TTCA Organic Composting Project in Attapeu province, Laos was constructed to produce organic fertilizer with an annual output of 34,000 tons from the treatment of cattle manure from livestock farmers in Attapeu province and from biodegradable waste residue such as Crotalaria spp. (a nitrogen fixation belonged to legume family which is used for rotation in sugarcane plantation), bagasse, mud and ash from a sugarcane processing factory in the site. The project is invested in and owned by TTC Attapeu Sugar Cane Sole Co., Ltd. The project aim is to avoid methane emissions through controlled aerobic decomposition in a windrow composting process of cattle manure, Crotalaria spp. waste and sugarcane processing waste (mud, ash, bagasse) in a landfill site.\r\nThe aerated composting process will avoid methane emissions and will also result in compost as a product that can be utilized as organic fertilizer for agricultural purposes. With financial support from the carbon credit, this project will demonstrate that the carbon credit finance mechanism can catalyze environmentally sustainable and financially viable waste management practices.\r\nIts operation will be made sustainable by covering the installation and operation cost through sale of compost and revenue from CDM. The CDM benefits would act as a means of subsidizing the cost of compost production to ensure the project’s financial sustainability. \r\nThe final compost obtained will be sold to organic sugarcane plantations in the province which lateral supply sugarcane to processing factory. The construction start date of the project was 28/01/2021 and was put into operation on the 16/11/2021. \r\nIt is estimated that an average of 10,823 tCO2e emission reductions will be generated annually and total emission reductions are 108,230 tCO2e in the 10 years’ fixed crediting period.","location":{"latitude":14.732216,"longi